    "durationMs": 347924,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL shortener is complete and fully verified end-to-end.\n\n**Implementation** (`src/main.rs`, axum 0.8.4 + sqlx/PostgreSQL):\n- `POST /links` — validates `url` with the `url` crate (absolute http/https, host required, printable-ASCII so it can safely sit in a `Location` header) and `code` (4–20 ASCII letters/digits/hyphens/underscores); returns 201 with the submitted URL unchanged, auto-generates an 8-char code when omitted, and returns 409 on duplicate custom codes (via `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`).\n- `GET /links/{code}` — 200 with `{code, url, clicks}` or 404 JSON error.\n- `GET /r/{code}` — atomic `UPDATE ... SET clicks = clicks + 1 RETURNING url` (increments exactly once), 302 with `Location`, 404 for unknown codes.\n- `GET /links` — items in `id` (creation) order with `total`.\n- All malformed-JSON/invalid-url/invalid-code paths return 422 JSON with an `error` field (bodies are parsed manually so even malformed JSON maps to 422, not axum's default 400).\n- Connection string comes from `DATABASE_URL` (retries up to 60s while Postgres starts); migrations are embedded via `sqlx::migrate!` and applied before the server binds.\n\n**Verified**: creation/validation/409s, redirect Location correctness, exact click counting, list ordering, and full persistence across a server restart (clicks went 2 → 3 after restart + redirect).\n\n**Deliverables**: executable `sh start.sh` (runs the prebuilt release binary, builds offline only if missing, serves foreground on 0.0.0.0:8000), README with start instructions, migration file. I truncated the test data afterward, so the database is empty and port 8000 is free for the test suite."
  }
